My nominations for best class to stand toe to toe are:

Wizard:
Stack a few score Confuse Monsters then poly to succubus and poke with 
+2 Magicbane. (Suggests silver dragon attire.)

Steal, seduce, confuse, then roll for what Magicbane wants to do this 
round.  And by the way regen spells for no food cost if melee gets boring.

Rogue:
Stay human and don't use anywhere near as much Confuse Monsters, but 
follow up Magicbane scare with Magicbane backstab.  Toss stacks of 
silver daggers at demons who wander off.  (Suggests silver dragon attire 
or a silver shield.)

OR

Stay human and Two Weapon the saber with an ordinary silver saber. 
(Suggests gray dragon attire or equivalent cloak.)

I can't seem to find a class combination that beats either of these two 
at these three tricks.  Non-wizards are crippled at stacking Confuse 
Monsters and Rogues do two-weapon saber better than anybody else when 
they're not being backstabbing cowards.

Is there a better hand to hand tactic?

